        "## 2. Dataset Selection\n",
        "\n",
        "The main dataset used in this project is **GoldRush Data (Implies speed & high-value insight)**, available on Kaggle:\n",
        "\n",
        "[GoldRush Data (Implies speed & high-value insight)](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rifatalam3/gold-price-trends?resource=download)\n",
        "\n",
        "This dataset provides the core **gold price time series**, including the main market variables needed to start the analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "To improve the model, a small set of external variables will be added. These were chosen because they have a clear economic connection to gold and can be explained without difficulty in the presentation.\n",
        "\n",
        "The variables included are:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Gold OHLCV data** from the Kaggle dataset as the main price series  \n",
        "- **10-year U.S. Treasury yield (DGS10)** to represent interest rates  \n",
        "- **10-year real yield (DFII10)** to capture the real-rate effect on gold  \n",
        "- **10-year breakeven inflation (T10YIE)** to reflect inflation expectations  \n",
        "- **Broad U.S. dollar index (DTWEXBGS)** since gold often moves with changes in the dollar  \n",
        "- **VIX** as an indicator of market stress and uncertainty  \n",
        "- **GVZ** as a measure of implied volatility in the gold market  \n",
        "- **S&P 500** to represent broader risk sentiment in financial markets  \n",
        "- **WTI oil prices** as a macroeconomic and inflation-related control  \n",
        "- **Geopolitical Risk Index (GPR)** to account for wars and geopolitical tension  \n",
        "- **Economic Policy Uncertainty (EPU)** to capture uncertainty linked to policy and institutions  \n",
        "\n",
        "This set is large enough to cover the main forces behind gold price movements without making the project unnecessarily cluttered."
      ],
