        "## 6. Training and optimization\n",
        "\n",
        "This section describes how the models are trained, how hyperparameters are selected, and how the final model is chosen. The goal goes  beyond lowering error. The training process must stay stable, reproducible, and fair across the different architectures.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 6.1 training Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "The project predicts two continuous targets.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **30-trading-day ahead log return**\n",
        "- **21-trading-day ahead realized volatility**\n",
        "\n",
        "The two targets use different scales, so both are standardized with training-set statistics. This prevents one target from controlling the loss only through a larger numerical range.\n",
        "\n",
        "The models use a joint loss, where return error and volatility error are learned together. This matches the main task of the project, which is forecasting future price movement\t\tand future market turbulence.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 6.2 loss Function\n",
        "\n",
        "The training loss uses **Huber loss** for each target.\n",
        "\n",
